TEXT -700 640 Left 1 ;MCU PWM (TP21 / TP22):\nINH = PWM_PHASEA_H, INL = PWM_PHASEA_L.\n1 = on.  DRV8323 6x mode.
TEXT -60 300 Left 1 ;SHA
TEXT -300 760 Left 1 ;Bgh/Bgl = DRV8323 gate drive: IDRIVEP source until VGS = VGSH/VGSL,\nIDRIVEN/ISTRONG sink when off. Rpd = 150k passive pull-downs (RPD).\nR20/R21 (0R) omitted.
TEXT 432 384 Left 1 ;motor phase A\n(ID_R hold)
TEXT 560 336 Left 1 ;CH1: SW, 10x probe
TEXT 560 576 Left 1 ;CH2: GL (GLA, TP39)
TEXT 256 160 Left 1 ;RC snubbers
TEXT -700 -560 Left 3 ;02 ONE LEG SWITCHING - phase A at 30 V, +5 A and -2.5 A (the two currents of an ID_R hold), what the DHO804 should show
TEXT -700 -512 Left 1 ;Question: switch-node edge rate, overshoot/undershoot, the body-diode step in the 200 ns dead time, and Miller-induced VGS on the off FET, at the real IDRIVE.\nStep 2 (Iph = +5 A, out of the leg = phase A in an ID_R hold): the HS turn-on is the hard edge (rising), HS turn-off is soft (the current pulls SW down).\nStep 1 (Iph = -2.5 A, into the leg = phase B or C in the same hold): roles swap, the LS turn-on is the hard edge (falling).\nPASS: Vds_pk < 80 V (80 % of 100 V), VgsL_miller < 2.3 V (VGS(th) min), and the shunt node back inside the CSA range (+-0.3 V) well before the sample.\nThe firmware open item "switch node NOT verified, a DMM read 75 V" is answered here: Vsw_pk is the true peak. Do not use the BM235 on SW (it averages a 25 kHz square).
TEXT 1000 -440 Left 1 ;HOW TO EDIT (.param lines below)\n  Vbus        bus voltage, V                          (30)\n  Iph         phase current at the edge, A            (stepped -2.5 / +5)\n  Isrc, Isnk  DRV8323 IDRIVEP / IDRIVEN, A            (p_drv_idrive code 15 = 1.0 / 2.0 A)\n  Vgsh, Vgsl  gate drive voltage, V                    (VGSH/VGSL, 11 V at VM > 13 V)\n  DT          dead time, s                             (TIM1 DTG=34 -> 200 ns)\n  T           PWM period, s                            (1/25 kHz, APP_PWM_FREQ_HZ)\n  Lpar        layout inductance per FET lead, H       (estimate; raise it if the scope rings lower)\n  Lgnd, Rgnd  probe ground lead: ~150 nH for the 15 cm clip, ~10 nH for the spring tip\n  BWscope     DHO804 bandwidth (70 MHz)\nMotor: an edge only sees the current (the winding is 9.44 uH / 98 mOhm, L/R = 96 us).
TEXT -700 880 Left 2 !.include ../lib/ISC030N10NM6_fit.lib\n.param Vbus=30 Iph=5 T={1/25k} DT=200n\n.param Isrc=1.0 Isnk=2.0 Vgsh=11 Vgsl=11\n.param Rsh=3m Lsh=0.6n Lpar=0.5n Lbulk=10n ESRbulk=0.3 Ccer=2.4u Lcer=0.3n\n.param Lgnd=150n Rgnd=20 Ctip=12p BWscope=70Meg\n.step param Iph list -2.5 5   ; LTspice runs list values in ascending order: step 1 = -2.5 A, step 2 = +5 A\n.nodeset V(GL)=11 V(GH)=0 V(SW)=0 V(VPROT)=30 V(DH)=30   ; DC starting guess only\n.tran 0 36u 0 1n\n.options plotwinsize=0\n.meas TRAN t_r10 WHEN V(SW)={0.1*Vbus} RISE=1 TD={T/8}\n.meas TRAN t_r90 WHEN V(SW)={0.9*Vbus} RISE=1 TD={T/8}\n.meas TRAN t_rise PARAM t_r90-t_r10\n.meas TRAN dvdt_rise_Vns PARAM 0.8*Vbus/t_rise/1e9\n.meas TRAN t_f90 WHEN V(SW)={0.9*Vbus} FALL=1 TD={T/2}\n.meas TRAN t_f10 WHEN V(SW)={0.1*Vbus} FALL=1 TD={T/2}\n.meas TRAN t_fall PARAM t_f10-t_f90\n.meas TRAN dvdt_fall_Vns PARAM 0.8*Vbus/t_fall/1e9
TEXT 260 880 Left 2 !.meas TRAN Vsw_pk MAX V(SW) FROM 2u\n.meas TRAN Vsw_min MIN V(SW) FROM 2u\n.meas TRAN Vsw_pk_scope MAX V(SW_SCOPE) FROM 2u\n.meas TRAN Vsw_min_scope MIN V(SW_SCOPE) FROM 2u\n.meas TRAN Vds_hs_pk MAX V(DH,SW) FROM 2u\n.meas TRAN Vds_ls_pk MAX V(SW,SL) FROM 2u\n.meas TRAN Vsw_dead1 FIND V(SW) AT {T/4}\n.meas TRAN Vsw_dead2 FIND V(SW) AT {3*T/4}\n.meas TRAN VgsL_miller MAX V(GL,SL) FROM {T/4+DT/2} TO {T/4+DT/2+1u}\n.meas TRAN VgsH_miller MAX V(GH,SW) FROM {3*T/4+DT/2} TO {3*T/4+DT/2+1u}\n.meas TRAN VgsL_pk_scope MAX V(GL_SCOPE) FROM {T/4+DT/2} TO {T/4+DT/2+1u}\n.meas TRAN Vshunt_max MAX V(SOURCE_A) FROM 2u\n.meas TRAN Vshunt_min MIN V(SOURCE_A) FROM 2u\n.meas TRAN Vshunt_on FIND V(SOURCE_A) AT {T/8}\n.meas TRAN Vgh_on FIND V(GH,SW) AT {T/2}\n.meas TRAN Vgl_on FIND V(GL) AT {T/8}
TEXT 1000 0 Left 1 ;Notes\n- Layout parasitics (Lpar, Lsh, Lcer, Lbulk) are estimates for a 2-layer-equivalent\n  TDSON-8 half-bridge; they set the ring frequency and overshoot, so treat Vsw_pk as\n  model-dependent and correct Lpar from the measured ring frequency.\n- V(SW) is the true node; V(SW_SCOPE) is what a 10x probe with its ground clip on a\n  70 MHz scope shows. Use the spring ground tip: the 15 cm clip adds its own ~100 MHz ring.\n- High-side VGS cannot be probed directly with earth-referenced probes: CH3 on GH (TP37)\n  and use CH3 - CH1 math. That math is only meaningful away from the edges.\n- MOSFET: ISC030N10NM6 behavioural VDMOS fit (lib/), not the Infineon model.\n  Checked against the datasheet: Rds(on) 2.55 mOhm, plateau 4.6 V, Qg 55 nC, Qgd 9.6 nC.\n- Bench: needs a PWM build at 30 V. Every approved scope so far is 12 V and the firmware\n  refuses ID / spin above 15 V: raising that is a separate, reviewed change.
